{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144534-how-do-you-think-the-ratkin-have-involved-themselves-in-the-solomon-islands","id":1144534,"title":"How do you think the Ratkin have involved themselves in the Solomon Islands?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-27T14:11:55-07:00","id":1144534,"title":"How do you think the Ratkin have involved themselves in the Solomon Islands?","content":"<b><a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2017/09/170927093329.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.sciencedaily.com/release...0927093329.htm</a></b><br /> <br /> <br /> Apparently there is a giant tree dwelling rat over in the Solomon Islands. Do you think the Ratkin that it produces are much different from the garden variety evil vermin?<br /> <br /> EDIT: A better title might have been how do you think Ratkin culture has evolved over in the Solomon Islands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-27-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T15:37:16-07:00","id":1144547,"title":"","content":"Serpents and serpentine 'dragons' are important clan and creator figures in the Solomons. So maybe some Naga or Zhoung Lung/Gumagan influence.<br /> <br /> Big part of Melanesian mythology is a boy ( or twins) of an abandoned woman who grows to kill fearsome human devouring ogres ( sometimes mannish others reptilian).<br /> <br /> Shark calling is a long tradition in parts of the Solomons.<br /> <br /> Only rat based myth I can find is a just-so story involving a rat and a rail.<br /> <br /> Given there are very few left and they are under threat from 90% of the Solomons forest being logged....theres probably very few ratkin.....and given that imtroduced rats have already killed off other giant rats on neighbouring islands by introducing diseases and competition.....maybe the ratkin there are quite willing to fight their more recently arrived 'cousins'.....perhaps with Nagah, Rokea or other aid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T23:05:06-07:00","id":1144648,"title":"","content":"I think its more that the Ratkin there would have developed far from cities and on islands distant to other populations. Likely they are independent, Nezumi or an offshoot of the Nezumi. I can imagine it took till relatively recently for the ratkin to have contact with other Fera besides the seldom Corax, Mokole, and maybe legendary questing Ratkin. But Island Rats could be interesting, and interesting they are from a different species of rodent, after all I imagine say 5k years ago the the Ratkin you encounter in say Egypt could have possibly have even been Mice since their current standard breed didn't spread out across the world till millennia later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}